{"name":"Green Garter","hex":"#61ba85","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"garter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A band worn around the leg to hold up a sock or stocking.","A bendlet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten with a garter","To wear a garter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garter","blocks":[{"text":"A garter is an article of clothing comprising a narrow band of fabric fastened about the leg to keep up stockings. In the 18th to 20th centuries, they were tied just below the knee, where the leg is most slender, to keep the stocking from slipping. The advent of elastic has made them less necessary from this functional standpoint, although they are still often worn for fashion. Garters have been widely worn by men and women, depending on fashion trends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garter","wikidata":"Q13742"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Garter_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Garter_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketch of a garter. The band goes around the leg, and the hook on the lower side attaches to the top of the stocking.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGarter_(cropped).tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg/500px-Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg/500px-Mlle._Rhea_Flask_LC-USZ62-99952.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_